## Document Access

**Search project knowledge before asserting feature state, schema or canonical values.**
Why: repo docs arrive as searched chunks, so a fact not retrieved is a fact not known.

**Never assert a current version, count or live value from synced docs; prompts tell Claude Code to read live files, and database claims are verified live, with the read-only connector where one is attached, before anything builds on them.**
Why: everything synced is a point-in-time snapshot, and files, versions and row counts move between syncs.

