## Supabase

Project `{{SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF}}` has two MCP connectors, and they are not interchangeable.

**Use `{{SUPABASE_RO_CONNECTOR}}` (read-only) for all live verification: SQL, logs, tables, migrations, extensions, function inspection, advisors, docs. Never ask the human to approve a query it could have run.**
Why: a read that cannot write cannot damage production, and a query run by hand is a wasted round trip.

**Never use `{{SUPABASE_RW_CONNECTOR}}` (writable) in a planning chat; if a task seems to need it, stop and say so.**
Why: it is reserved for Claude Code sessions doing rolled-back behavioral probes and deploys.

**The read-only connector bypasses RLS, so its counts are fleet-wide; scope to `{{OWNER_USER_ID}}` when a per-user figure matters.**
Why: an unscoped count covers every user's orders while reading like one user's.

**A feature group missing from the read-only connector (project URL, keys, type generation) is not a reason to switch connectors.**
Why: planning never needs those groups enough to justify write access.

**Schema changes are applied in the dashboard SQL editor, never by CLI push, and a function's deploy command goes in the same prompt that edits it.**
Why: the CLI's migration history conflicts with hand-applied changes, and Edge Functions do not deploy on git push.
<!-- END:supabase -->

