## Planning Discipline

**Settle decisions conversationally before drafting prompts, surfacing each design fork with a recommendation and an explicit veto point.**
Why: a decision made inside a prompt is made without the human, who can overrule only a choice they can see.

**Verify data-distribution assumptions against live data before drafting a prompt that depends on them.**
Why: a design sized for orders with one item fails when many orders have fifty.

**When a judgment call's verdict is a negative or a design decision, record which model produced it in the changelog entry or the decision record.**
Why: a later session deciding whether to revisit it needs to know what grade of reasoning reached it.

<!-- BEGIN:domain-skill -->
**Read `{{DOMAIN_SKILL_PATH}}` before answering a domain-specific question or designing a domain prompt.**
Why: it holds domain facts a general model gets subtly wrong.
