## Session Close-Out

**Propose a close-out unprompted when a unit of work is closed and verified: a decision shipped and verified, a slice landed with its record written, or a deploy pin recorded.**
Why: that is when everything in this chat has a home in the repo; mid-unit, some state lives only here.

**Also propose one after roughly six to eight Claude Code round trips, or when answering needs re-reading state from earlier in the session.**
Why: either means the context is filling up.

At close-out:
- Say which unit just closed and what the next session's first prompt would be.
- Name the model for the next planning chat: reasoning-grade by default, top-tier only for a critical design moment.
- On agreement, draft the handoff to the convention in CLAUDE.md's Document Map; each handoff fully supersedes the previous one.
- A new session reads, on arrival, the roadmap's sequence for the epic plus the newest handoff.

**A detour that closes within its own session gets no handoff.**
Why: its record is already its changelog entries or commits, its decision record and any roadmap residuals.
